s seen as the orange and red curves achieving a lower training error while the test error increases. Lastly, again by comparing Figure 4b and 4c, we see that the compositional mapping of the split architecture is the only mapping which generalizes well (near 0 training and test error). Thus, even in this more complex setting, we see the negative effect a shared hidden layer has on the generalization of the network (comparing the blue and green curves)."
